\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thee, Jesus, Thee, the sinner's Friend,
\par I follow on to apprehend,
\par Renew the glorious strife;
\par Divinely confident and bold,
\par With faith's strong arm on Thee lay hold,
\par Thee, my eternal life.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Prisoner of hope, to Thee I turn,
\par And, calmly confident, I mourn,
\par And pray, and weep for Thee;
\par Tell me Thy love, Thy secret tell,
\par Thy mystic name in me reveal,
\par Reveal Thyself in me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Descend, pass by me, and proclaim,
\par O Lord of hosts, Thy glorious name-
\par The Lord, the gracious Lord,
\par Longsuffering, merciful, and kind;
\par The God who always bears in mind
\par His everlasting word.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Plenteous He is in truth and grace;
\par He wills that all the fallen race
\par Should turn, repent, and live;
\par His pardoning grace for all is free;
\par Transgression, sin, iniquity,
\par He freely doth forgive.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Mercy he doth for thousands keep;
\par He goes and seeks the one lost sheep;
\par And brings His wanderer  home;
\par And every soul that sheep might be:
\par Come then, my Lord, and gather me,
\par My Jesus, quickly come!
\par                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

